        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Sealing a marble floor well means testing the tiles, the grout and the traffic lanes separately, using an impregnating sealer rated for both stone and grout, and wiping every section completely dry before it can cure on top. Films and waxes do not belong on a marble floor.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            After that, the floor's protection depends on habits: walk-off mats, frequent dust mopping, a pH-neutral cleaner, a squeegee in the shower, and a water test twice a year. Reseal the lanes and grout that absorb, leave the rest alone, and remember that slip resistance comes from the tile's finish, not from the sealer.
          </p>
